Use the UL command to upload a file to the system.  In order to upload a
file, you will first need to have selected a file transfer protocol via
CONFIG.  Once you enter UL, you will have to enter a name for the file,
an appropriate, brief description and the name(s) of the computer(s) with
which the file will work. (Enter All or Any if the file can be used with any
computer: i.e. a text file)  Then enter you terminal's upload mode or hit
CTRL-X to abort.
